  "language": "en",
  "text": "So there's one more thing that I want to add. I play ice hockey, and I used to play a forward position, center ice. And when I got my shoulder hurt, I loved the game so much, the only position I could play was goalie. And my eyes were opened up, and I realized that this is applicable to all life situations, especially in business. I was able to scan the whole ice and see from a goalie's perspective, almost like a bird's eye view, what it was like when players with enough talent to be destructive to their own ability did not use their teammates. And I realized I was so laser-focused on shooting that puck and scoring a lot of goals, I could have done a lot better job passing the puck and building confidence in my teammates. And so that one-dimensional way of thinking in business, yes, you can save money, but the pie grows. The pie here, in our mind, we think that there's only so much work available for all these contractors when it can expand and grow continually. And so my encouragement to anyone that's thinking, how can marketing help me? Can I afford to spend $100 a day? It depends on the capacity you have and the desire you want to truly grow with a good team versus doing everything yourself and running your mind ragged.",
